  "term": "disulfiram",
  "definition": "Disulfiram is a medication used to deter alcohol use by changing how the body processes alcohol. If a person drinks alcohol after taking it, acetaldehyde builds up and can cause unpleasant reactions such as flushing, nausea, breathing difficulty, and low blood pressure.",
